summary:
  A level asked for while a device has not yet answered is never sent to
  it, so an alarm's level misses a device that is slow to take the stream.

history:
  A device that is still being asked is not sent a level any more: it may
  refuse, and then it was turned down for nothing. But an alarm asks for
  its level right after it starts the station, 400 ms before the timer
  sends it, and a television took 389 ms to answer (2026-11-12). Dropped,
  the level would leave a speaker that was turned down the night before
  whispering through the alarm. What was asked for is kept for the device
  and goes out with its answer.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CastLogic.js

find:
      for (var k in s.pending) s.owed[k] = pct;

replace:
      for (var k in s.pending) delete s.owed[k];

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_castlogic.qml::test_a_level_asked_for_while_a_device_is_asked_goes_out_with_its_answer.
